  "facts": [
    "The Manhattan Bridge, opened December 31, 1909, was the first suspension bridge to employ a Warren truss, a design that later influenced many long-span bridges worldwide.",
    "Designed by Leon Moisseiff, the bridge’s 1,480‑ft main span rests on two 350‑ft towers, with 1,400 vertical suspender cables carrying a seven‑lane roadway and four subway tracks.",
    "Between 1982 and 2004, the bridge underwent a massive reconstruction after uneven subway train loads caused it to tilt, restoring its structural integrity for modern traffic."
